;; rsi's divergences from rustc 1.99.1 on ci (doc/rust/EVAL.md §9; doc/rust/RUST-EVAL-SURVEY.md, "As built: RE4 (write-ahead)"):
;; the classes every program of bin/rsi check that does not pass falls into, each with why and where it was decided, in
;; test/goi/divergences.edn's format. A program's class is the first whose :match finds its result and reason ("RESULT REASON",
;; as test/rust/check-linux-amd64.edn writes them); :nondet (the judge's own runs differ) is a result, not a class. bin/rsi
;; divergences judges the recorded check against them. Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :threads
  :title "threads (deferred: ci runs no threads)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "std::thread::spawn starts a thread by musl's pthread_create, whose clone is assembly: ci's back end has no threads (C's class threads, doc/c/SPEC.md §6.5; C++'s); RES7 (a) left threads out of v1"
  :decided "RES7 (a); C's §6.5"
  :match [#"undefined function __clone" #"failed to spawn thread"]}
 {:id :speed
  :title "speed: programs beyond the check's budget"
  :kind :design
  :why "an interpreter of nodes is 10 to 100 times slower than rustc's -O0 code (C's, C++'s and goi's class of the same name)"
  :decided "C's CS107 (a); survey §14"
  :match [#"^fail differ status timeout"]}
 {:id :not-lowered
  :title "a stub of std reached (f16)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "std's functions the lowering does not take (core's f16) are stubs that abort with their name (EVAL.md §8); f16 and f128 at RE5"
  :decided "RES24 (a)"
  :match [#"rsi: not lowered"]}
]
